// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: omkar72
// Date: 2020-10-30 | Modified: 2023-02-28
// ATT&CK: execution, lateral-movement, T1569, T1021
// Description: Detects user accept agreement execution in psexec commandline
// False positives:
//   - Administrative scripts.
// References:
//   - https://www.fireeye.com/blog/threat-research/2020/10/kegtap-and-singlemalt-with-a-ransomware-chaser.html
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_sysinternals_psexec_execution.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "\\psexec.exe" or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "psexec.c"
